The court must ensure that the law is followed in ascertaining the free will of the detained or missing person;
(i) If a detained or missing person expresses their wish to not go back to the alleged detainer or the natal family, then the person must be released immediately without any further delay;
(j) The court must acknowledge that some intimate partners may face social stigma and a neutral stand of the law would be detrimental to the fundamental freedoms of the appellant.

The protection granted to intimate partners must be with a view to maintain their privacy and dignity;
Yash Pal And Another vs State Of Haryana And Others on 9 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/185458725/
